WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:14.546
Sign in as the business owner.

2
00:00:14.646 --> 00:00:21.058
Open Inventory, then Stock levels. It lists every product and how many you have in the current branch.

3
00:00:21.158 --> 00:00:26.249
The branch is shown at the top of the screen. Switch it to see another branch.

4
00:00:26.349 --> 00:00:30.009
Each row has a status: Healthy, Low or Out of stock.

5
00:00:30.109 --> 00:00:35.089
The Low tab lists items that are running short, so you know what to reorder.

6
00:00:37.019 --> 00:00:40.734
The Out tab shows items that have run out completely.

7
00:00:42.635 --> 00:00:45.581
Go back to All stock to see everything.

8
00:00:45.682 --> 00:00:48.848
Narrow the list by category, brand or unit.

9
00:00:52.374 --> 00:00:54.990
Or search by product name or SKU.

10
00:00:56.593 --> 00:01:01.848
This product shows Low. Say a new delivery just arrived. Click Adjust on its row.

11
00:01:02.753 --> 00:01:07.074
Add stock is selected. Enter how many to add, not the new total.

12
00:01:07.174 --> 00:01:11.384
Every change needs a reason. It is saved in the stock history.

13
00:01:12.286 --> 00:01:15.233
Click Adjust stock to apply the change.

14
00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:22.184
The stock now shows 31 and the status has changed from Low to Healthy.

15
00:01:24.086 --> 00:01:29.617
Open Stock Adjustments for the full history of every change, with who made it and why.

16
00:01:32.318 --> 00:01:37.575
Use Stock levels to watch your shelves, and adjustments to keep the numbers true.
